+# Filtering the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope, Free-Text Veterinarian Search Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, on the ground that owner search already demonstrates paged prefix search. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so its provenance stayed open.
+
+A request now asks for the veterinarian directory to be filtered by specialty. Read against NG-9 as written, the request either breaches the row or reopens it by implication. The owner has decided the row instead (2026-09-06).
+
+The same request reinstates the machine-readable veterinarian listing, withdrawn as `REQ-VET-002` on 2026-07-31, as a supported surface. That reinstatement is recorded in the PRD under a fresh requirement.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 as written.** Decline the filter. Rejected by the owner: the directory already shows the specialties, so filtering on them adds no entity to the search surface.
+2. **Retire NG-9.** Open search across pets, visits, and veterinarians. Rejected: free-text search over further entities repeats the owner-search pattern without teaching anything new, which is the row's original reason.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined; filtering the directory on an attribute it already displays is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 covers free-text search only. Selecting from a listing by an attribute that listing already shows is a distinct capability and is in scope. The narrowing is bounded to the veterinarian directory and its specialties; it grants nothing for pets or visits.
+
+The filter is an address contract in this round. Neither the page nor the machine-readable listing gains a form, a dropdown, or any other page control. A visible control is a separate request.
+
+A future request touching NG-9 again proceeds only on an owner decision recorded at intake.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation; its rationale now carries the narrowing and its date.
+- Filtering the directory by specialty is specified as `REQ-VET-003`, which also covers the reinstated machine-readable listing.
+- `REQ-VET-002` stays withdrawn and its id is not reused, so existing links keep resolving to the withdrawal.
+- Pet search and visit search stay declined. A request for either reads as a fresh narrowing, not as precedent.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the requirement the narrowing admits.
