+# Paging Links Carry the Specialty as Link-Expression Parameters
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VET-003` requires a filtered veterinarian listing to stay navigable across pages, so every paging link on the page must carry the specialty name. That name arrives in the query string, and any caller chooses it.
+
+The paging links in `vetList.html` and `ownersList.html` concatenate the page number into a string inside a link expression. Concatenating a caller-supplied name emits it unencoded, so a name holding `&`, `#`, or `+` breaks the link and corrupts the filter.
+
+Thymeleaf renders a link parameter whose value is null as a bare, valueless parameter rather than omitting it. Passing the specialty unconditionally therefore changes the addresses an unfiltered listing renders.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Concatenate the specialty into the link string.** Matches the existing idiom, but emits caller-supplied text unencoded into the address.
+2. **One link expression per link, passing the specialty always.** Encodes correctly, but every paging link on an unfiltered page gains `specialty=`. The blank value reads as no filter, so the listing stays right. The addresses change on a surface this round leaves otherwise untouched.
+3. **Spell out both link forms and select between them** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Every paging link in `vetList.html` is a link expression with parameters, never a concatenated string. Each link selects between a form naming the specialty and a form omitting it, on whether the model attribute is null. The controller publishes that attribute as null when no filter is active.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Caller-supplied text is URL-encoded on every paging link, so a specialty name holding a URL delimiter survives paging. A test asserts it.
+- An unfiltered listing renders the addresses it rendered before the filter existed. A test asserts that no paging link names a specialty.
+- Each of the five paging links spells out both forms, so the template repeats the branch five times. The cost is accepted for one page.
+- A later listing that carries a filter through paging follows this shape. Owner search does not carry its search term today — see [system-design.md § Known Defects](../system-design.md#known-defects).
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — `VetController` and the surfaces it serves.
+- [ADR: Filtering the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope](2026-09-06-non-goal-vet-specialty-filter.md) — the product decision this serves.
+- [ADR: Specialty-Filtered Veterinarian Reads Stay Outside the Vets Cache](2026-09-06-vet-cache-excludes-filtered-reads.md) — the sibling decision on the read path.
